Spec: Segments

Purpose:
  Turn a video of any length into candidate stretches a person can choose.

Owns:
  ./segments.rs

Must:
  Scene changes come from ffmpeg at a scene threshold of 0.3.
  The stretches between those times are the candidates, including the opening stretch.
  A stretch shorter than 1 second merges into the previous one.
  Each candidate records source, start, and end.

Must not:
  Encode video.
  Drop the opening stretch.
  Call the network.
  Save a post.

Scenario: short stretch merges
  Given a scene stretch of half a second after an earlier stretch
  When segments are built
  Then the half-second stretch is part of the previous candidate

Scenario: opening remains
  Given a video whose first scene is the opening
  When segments are built
  Then the opening is a candidate
  And no post file is written
